TITLE:: LinkCPS
summary:: UGen that gets and sets the cycles per second of the server's Link clock
categories:: UGens>Clock, Streams-Patterns-Events
related:: Classes/LinkPhase, Classes/LinkClock, Classes/LinkJump

DESCRIPTION::

An UGen that gets and sets the CPS (cycles per second) of the server's Link clock, such that the CPS can be modulated through a signal.
Ableton Link internally uses BPM which gets converted by the server to CPS by dividing the BPM value by 60.
See LINK::Classes/LinkPhase:: for examples.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: kr
Returns the current CPS of the Link clock of the server.
If the server clock has not been enabled via LINK::Classes/LinkPhase#*start::, it will return MATH::-1.0::.
argument:: change
If this value is MATH::>0.0::, the CPS (second argument) will be used to set for the Link clock and published to the other clients.
argument:: cps
The CPS to be set.
Ableton Link uses BPM internally and only allows bpm values between MATH::[20, 999]::, which translates to MATH::[\frac{1}{3}, 16.65]:: cps.

NOTE::
See also LINK::Classes/LinkPhase#*setCPS::
::
